For every OpenSCAD model, I highly recommend using the **Nightly** development version of OpenSCAD. It utilizes the modern **Manifold Engine**, making it vastly faster and significantly more stable than older OpenSCAD versions running on the classic CGAL Engine.

With the Nightly build, projects will render much quicker, and you won't encounter bugs or crashes with complex geometry (like nested or overlapping `hull()` operations). 

*(Note: Online versions like OpenSCAD Playground often rely on older backend engines and will struggle or crash when trying to render these complex geometries. Stick to the Nightly version for the best experience).*

You can find the **Nightly** version of OpenSCAD for Windows, Mac, and Linux here:
👉 https://openscad.org
